      "parallelizable": false,
      "_comment": "EmuquUITests runs serially (parallelizable: false). Measured 2026-08-19: under three parallel simulator clones SettingsNavigationUITests failed in roughly half of full runs and passed every time in isolation. Unit tests keep their parallelism.  ||  WIRED 2026-08-25. This plan was previously referenced by nothing, so testExecutionOrdering random had never taken effect. It was tried and reverted once: random ordering found two real defects in the unit target (both since fixed), but three dashboard tests (PermissionDenialUITests.testDashboardSurfacesGuidanceWhenHealthKitDenied, EmuquUITests.testDashboardShowsRecoveryScoreSection, AccessibilityAuditUITests.testDashboardTabPassesAccessibilityAudit) read whatever the shared archive happened to hold, so shuffling made them a coin flip. The stated precondition was 'do not wire this until the UI target gets a hermetic archive too'. That landed 2026-08-25: AppLaunchRecovery.removeStoredSessionData() wipes the archive and raw-RR backup directories under -UITests-FreshInstall, which all 14 launching suites pass, before SessionArchive.shared is first touched."
    }
  ],
  "version": 1,
  "_comment": "EmuquUITests runs serially (parallelizable: false). Measured 2026-08-19: under three parallel simulator clones SettingsNavigationUITests failed in roughly half of full runs and passed every time in isolation — the tab tap silently not taking on a contended host, surfacing several steps later as 'More menu should list Settings' while the app sat on the Dashboard. Unit tests keep their parallelism; only the UI target, which drives a whole app per worker, gives it up.  ||  2026-08-26: the previous text here said this plan was NOT WIRED and that testExecutionOrdering had never taken effect. That stopped being true on 2026-08-25 — Emuqu.xcscheme references this plan (see its <TestPlans> block) and the testTargets comment below records the change. Two comments in one file disagreeing about whether a gate is active is worse than either of them alone, so the stale one is gone. Random ordering is live for both targets; the UI target became safe under shuffling when AppLaunchRecovery.removeStoredSessionData() started wiping the archive and raw-RR backup directories under -UITests-FreshInstall, which all 14 launching suites pass."
}
